          "text": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: inherit; font-variant-caps: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\">Alonso Álvarez de Pineda, during a 1519 Spanish expedition\nseeking a water passage to the Orient through the Gulf, described this harbor\nand gave it the name Bahía del Espíritu Santo.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: inherit; font-variant-caps: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: inherit; font-variant-caps: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\">Successive Spanish explorers\nsought this \"Holy Grail\" along the Gulf Coast, failing until a 1693\nexpedition concluded that what is now called Mobile Bay was the fabled Bay of\nthe Holy Spirit.</span></p>"
